content:
Two faults. Both are height, and the first one is a hundred copies of a single
element.

RULE FOR THIS RUN: your first tool call must be deploy. Ship a fix, then measure
it, then fix again. Twenty steps.

  deploy(css, js)             splices your block in, publishes it, returns errors
  measure(js, width, query)   runs a JavaScript arrow function against your page
  parent(js, width, query)    the same, against the original
  done(summary)               when the checks pass

Your block is at the end of this brief and is on the page now.

# 1. The write-up cell is 32px taller than the original's, a hundred times over

At /z/?hero=where&zone=ZONE+200, 1440px, with the record table loaded:

                       original   rebuild
    .wu (the write-up)     112       144
    tr.wrote row           126       159
    tr.rep row              72        73
    table                14,914    17,977
    page                 16,655    20,002

Same 13px type. The original's line-height is 20.15px, yours is 19.5px, so it is
not leading: your block simply shows more of the mechanic's text before it clips.
The original clips the write-up to a fixed height and fades the last line, with
the full text still reachable by opening the case sheet.

Measure the original's .wu: its height, its max-height, its overflow, whether it
uses a line clamp and at how many lines, and what its fade is. Then match it.

Do not delete the write-up or its gloss button. The mechanic's own words are the
reason this table exists. Clip them the way the original clips them.

    td padding is also 5px 10px here against the original's 4px 10px.

# 2. Three blocks the original does not have, above the tabs

    rebuild top-level children of <main>:
      znarrow 30, hero-root 784, tip 0, card.ask 59, khint 17, out 0,
      credit 28, views 18803

    original:
      hero 837, tabs 104, freshness 19, credit 19, then the panels

`.card.ask` (59px) and `.khint` (17px) sit between the instrument and the tabs
and have no counterpart in the original, whose "aim at" line lives inside the
instrument. `znarrow` is 30px above everything. Read what each of the three says
before you remove anything: if it carries text the original carries elsewhere,
move it there rather than deleting it. If it carries nothing the original has,
say so in your summary and take it out.

    credit is 28 here against 19 there, which is spacing.

# The checks, before you call done

  1. At ?hero=where&zone=ZONE+200, 1440: tr.wrote within 10% of 126, the table
     within 10% of 14,914, and documentElement.scrollHeight within 10% of 16,655.
  2. The write-up still shows the mechanic's words, clipped and faded like the
     original's, and the gloss button under it still works.
  3. Still true, all of them, and measure each: /z/?zone=ZONE+500&operator=CALA
     reads "219 reports, left wing, Continental Airlines Inc. 1,757,608 set
     aside." at 1440 and 390; unfiltered reads the 1,757,827 sentence with the
     published-to date at both widths; 390 has no page error, #count above the
     fold, body scrollWidth 390, no .rail visible; 1440 has the open rail within
     10% of 508 with its reading paragraph, svg within 5% of 628 x 138, one
     sentence carrier in .ipad and it is #count, #vstrip at or under 130px with
     16 .vtab and 16 [role=tab], no page error, 18 controls, 18 starter
     questions, 4 .rail, 16 section.panel.

Put the measured numbers in the summary.

Do not undo the phone layout, the case sheet overlay, the record stepper or the
aria-labels. Prefix every new name.

--- YOUR CURRENT BLOCK ---

